==English==

===Etymology===
From {{Arab.}} {{Arab|[[سيد|سَيّد]]}}, meaning master, sir, mister.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Arabic given name, meaning "master".
# {{Islam}} an [[honorific]] [[title]] [[borne]] by male [[descendant]]s of the [[prophet]] [[Muhammad]].
# In Arabic it is also a form of address of a [[male]] [[dignitary]], with the feminine form being {{Arab|[[سيدة]]}}.
# Arabic equvalent to [[Mr.]] in English.

